@@ -82,6 +82,12 @@ npm test
 
 `test/smoke.js` launches the standalone file in Chromium and verifies the important migration boundary: contracts, JSON downloads, current spec validation, responsive behavior, rails/toolbars, edit mode, keyboard navigation and browser errors.
 
+`test/regression.js` also checks malformed imports, preservation of named theme presets in downloaded JSON, immediate JSON-editor blur, retained invalid drafts, undo/redo timing, open-panel responsive layout, and saving on reload. Both suites run with `npm test`.
+
+Theme imports use standard JSON. Named style definitions are retained when exporting; other theme settings are read into the workbench's supported controls. JSON drafts are validated when leaving the editor, and invalid drafts remain available for correction. Autosave reports storage failures and flushes pending session changes when the page is hidden or left.
+
+Unfinished JSON drafts are kept separately when switching between theme and spec in the tool panel (for the current page session). Ctrl/Cmd+Enter applies the active draft immediately; Ctrl/Cmd+Z inside text fields uses native text undo. Saved-session recovery and spec comparison reject malformed structure before replacing current state.
+
 GitHub Actions runs the same smoke audit on pushes and pull requests.
 
 ## Repository layout
